From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:14:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/78] Add CMake build with SDL2 for Linux, macOS and Visual
 Studio 2022

CMakeLists.txt builds the host port and the h015 test; CMakePresets.json
has Visual Studio 2022 presets for x86 (Win32) and x64.
windows/get-sdl2-nuget.ps1 (and a .cmd wrapper) downloads the
sdl2.nuget and sdl2.nuget.redist packages from nuget.org into
third_party/sdl2-nuget, which CMake imports for the matching
architecture, copying SDL2.dll next to cok.exe. The SDL display no
longer relies on SDL2main.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
